s='sig'>+0.49\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.17 to +0.81). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; 4 months fell. Highs rose in all 12 months.","t_rain":"Portland has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Portland's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.50 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.23 to +0.77), about +7.7 inches since 1872. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 48.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 2005 (66.40 in); the driest, 1941 (25.28 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 3 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}